 "deviations": [
  "The instance role (multiomics-inputs-20261004-1940) cannot write under rapidglm/; adding a scoped policy was refused by the session permission check, so pikachu pulled checkpoints hourly (instance-side rsync under nice 19) and results over SSH and pushed them to AWS object storage.",
  "Docker on the instance (29.1.3, containerd store) reports the image ID as the manifest digest, pikachu as the config digest; the first worker start stopped on that check before any test or run, and was restarted with both digests accepted. Binary and library SHA-256 equal on both hosts.",
  "The first hourly checkpoint push at 12:01 UTC was skipped (rsync exit 24 on a tile being renamed); relay v2 skips *.tmp from 12:02 UTC.",
  "From 2026-10-23 13:57 UTC pikachu CPUs 0-15 were capped at 2.2 GHz by the user after silent corruption on CPUs 12-15. My heavy pikachu work ran on CPUs 0-7 (and 0-1 after 09:25 UTC); every copied file is checked by SHA-256 at both ends.",
  "Coordinator limits: pikachu jobs on CPUs 0-7 under nice, then at most 2 threads on CPUs 0-1 until 2026-10-24 00:00 UTC; never the timing lock.",
  "The controlling session ended twice (about 17:24 and 22:20 UTC on 2026-10-23). The first end stopped relay v3, so no hourly checkpoint copy ran between 17:05 and 18:15 UTC; relay v4 (detached from 18:15 UTC) checks the hourly copies by SHA-256 at the instance, pikachu and AWS object storage. A detached finisher (scripts/finisher.sh) did the end-of-run checks and the termination. The runs on the instance were not affected."
 ]
